```

If `eval_str=True` is used, `inspect.signature` will try to evaluate the annotations. If it fails, it raises a `NameError`.

If we change `eval_str=True` to `eval_str=False`, then `annotation` will be a string if it was stringified. Then `get_typed_annotation` will handle it:

```python
def get_typed_annotation(annotation: Any, globalns: Dict[str, Any]) -> Any:
    if isinstance(annotation, str):
        annotation = ForwardRef(annotation)
        annotation = evaluate_forwardref(annotation, globalns, globalns)
        if annotation is type(None):
            return None
    return annotation
```

